From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shahed <jamshidalinezhadian@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:40:00 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] camera2: pass the inverse-display flag to
 getRotationTransform

Android 15 added a bool enableTransformInverseDisplay parameter to
CameraUtils::getRotationTransform(); the legacy shim's JNI still made
the three-argument call and libandroid_runtime failed to compile:

  error: too few arguments to function call, expected 4, have 3

Camera2Client and Camera3Device pass true unless the desktop-windowing
rotation override is set, which the legacy shim never uses. Pass true,
which keeps the Android 14 behaviour (the flag was always set there).

Change-Id: I7c2e5a9d4b1f8e3a6c0d2b5f9e8a7c4d1b3e6f20
---
 .../android_hardware_camera2_legacy_LegacyCameraDevice.cpp  | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/jni/android_hardware_camera2_legacy_LegacyCameraDevice.cpp b/core/jni/android_hardware_camera2_legacy_LegacyCameraDevice.cpp
index 0de5e0f..f5990dc 100644
--- a/core/jni/android_hardware_camera2_legacy_LegacyCameraDevice.cpp
+++ b/core/jni/android_hardware_camera2_legacy_LegacyCameraDevice.cpp
@@ -721,8 +721,12 @@ static jint LegacyCameraDevice_nativeSetSurfaceOrientation(JNIEnv* env, jobject
 
     int32_t transform = 0;
 
+    // Android 15 made the inverse-display flag a parameter. Camera2Client and Camera3Device
+    // default it to true and clear it only for the desktop-windowing rotation override,
+    // which the legacy shim never uses; true keeps the see-through preview of Android 14.
     if ((err = CameraUtils::getRotationTransform(staticMetadata,
-            /*mirrorMode: MIRROR_MODE_AUTO*/ 0, /*out*/&transform)) != NO_ERROR) {
+            /*mirrorMode: MIRROR_MODE_AUTO*/ 0, /*enableTransformInverseDisplay*/ true,
+            /*out*/&transform)) != NO_ERROR) {
         ALOGE("%s: Invalid rotation transform %s (%d)", __FUNCTION__, strerror(-err),
                 err);
         return err;
-- 
